{title: Consider the Lilies}
{subtitle: Matthew 6:25–34}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 82}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Abmaj7] | [Eb] | [Abmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]I lie awake and count the [Abmaj7]bills, I count the hours till day [Eb]
I write the lists of all I [Abmaj7]need and the lists of what I'll [Eb]say
[Cm]Then in the morn[Bb]ing on the [Abmaj7]step a sparrow comes to [Eb]sing
[Cm]He doesn't know [Bb]where lunch will come [Abmaj7]from, he isn't wor[Eb]rying
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Look at [Abmaj7]the birds of the air
[Eb]They do not [Cm]sow or reap or [Bb]gather into barns
And yet your [Abmaj7]heavenly Father feeds [Eb]them
Are [Cm]you not worth [Bb]far more than [Abmaj7]they
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Abmaj7] | [Abmaj7] | [Eb] | [Abmaj7] |
| [Eb] | [Abmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Consider how the lilies [Abmaj7]of the field grow [Eb]
They do not labor or spin [Abmaj7]
[Cm]Yet not even Solomon in [Abmaj7]all his splendor
Was dressed like one [Eb]of these
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
But seek first his kingdom and his [Bb]righteousness
And [Cm]all these things will be [Eb]given to you as well
So [Abmaj7]do not worry a[Bb]bout tomorrow
For to[Cm]morrow will worry a[Abmaj7]bout itself
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Your heavenly Father knows [Cm]that you need them all [Abmaj7]
Your heavenly Father [Eb][Abmaj7]knows
{end_of_verse}

